# Content separation rules

## The critical rule
Public policy content and Acme operational content must ALWAYS be stored, retrieved, and displayed separately.

## Source domains
- `public_policy` — guidance grounded in publicly available UK council tax guidance principles
- `acme_operations` — fictional Acme City Council internal handling instructions

## In the content bundle
- public_policy guidance cards live in `src/versions/v1/public-policy/`
- acme_operations guidance cards live in `src/versions/v1/acme-operations/`
- NEVER combine them into a single file

## In the API
- Guidance cards carry a `source_domain` field
- Always include source_domain in API responses for guidance content

## In the UI
- The guidance panel must visually distinguish public_policy from acme_operations cards
- Use a visible label or badge for each source domain
- The system must never present Acme operational rules as if they were public policy
